#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# numerator

#% text
# `numerator(x)` gives the numerator of a rational number, or the product of the factors of `x` with positive exponents.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# For a product, factors with negative exponents (such as `1/y` or `y^(-2)`) are left out; a sum is one factor and is not combined over a common denominator.

#% item
# `numerator` is listable.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
numerator(6/15)
#% output
#= 2

#% cell
numerator(7)
#% output
#= 7

#% cell
numerator(x^2/(y*z))
#% output
#= x^2

#% cell
numerator((x + 1)/(x - 1))
#% output
#= 1 + x

#% subsection
# Scope

#% text
# A sum of fractions is not brought over a common denominator; combine it first:

#% cell
numerator(1/x + 1/y)
#% output
#= x^-1 + y^-1

#% cell
numerator(together(1/x + 1/y))
#% output
#= x + y

#% subsection
# Properties and relations

#% text
# The fraction is the quotient of numerator and denominator:

#% cell
numerator(22/8)/denominator(22/8)
#% output
#= 11/4

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `denominator`, `together`, `cancel`
